(Primes and perfect squares, all numbers: this whole program compiles to a native ELF (Zoomy 5.1).)
make checked a global number
Create an array named primes with 30 slots
Let a number be called found

(Give back 1 when n is prime, otherwise 0.)
define is_prime with n:
    if n is less than 2:
        give back 0
    for d from 2 to square root of n:
        add 1 to checked
        if n mod d is 0:
            give back 0
    give back 1

(Find the first 30 primes.)
Let a number be called candidate
set candidate to 2
until found is 30:
    if is_prime(candidate) is 1:
        set item found of primes to candidate
        add 1 to found
    add 1 to candidate

Let a number be called total
for each p in primes:
    add p to total
print "The first ", found, " primes end with ", the last of primes, "."
print "Their sum is ", total, "; I tested ", checked, " divisors."

(Greatest common divisor, by recursion.)
define gcd with m and k:
    if k is 0:
        give back m
    give back gcd(k, m mod k)
print "gcd(84, 36) = ", gcd(84, 36)

Let a flag be called lucky
set lucky to total is above 1000
print "Is the sum above 1000? ", lucky
